  "title": "Engine window step 1: upstream NInfer head against the shipped runtime on the RTX 5090 lane",
  "generated_utc": "2026-09-24T05:50:00Z",
  "status": "passed",
  "question": "Before merging 202 upstream commits into the fork both mainline lanes build from, does upstream head improve the RTX 5090 lane on the gates that need no durable layer, and does the generic export refusal EXP-047 left unexplained depend on upstream at all?",
  "answer": "No on both counts. On the same appliance, weights and serving arguments, upstream head matches the shipped runtime within noise on prefill and on decode rounds per second, and its decode rate moves only with MTP acceptance on content its newer chat template renders differently. It keeps less prefix reuse on this product's workloads: 0 of 4 fanout branches reuse the base (4 of 4 shipped) and 4 of 8 two-session continuations re-prefill from root (2 of 8 shipped). The export refusal lives in the fork: its own store overwrites the engine's named skip reason with the generic one, and upstream has no durable export to compare. The shipped arm reproduced the refusal at shutdown in this window: saved 2, refused 2, state lost.",
  "decision": {
    "merge": "deferred",
    "reason": "The merge buys no measured lane gain and costs a re-architecture port: 111 unmerged paths (27 take upstream, 44 hunk merges, 40 ports into upstream's restructured model, context-cache and serve layers), clean-merge semantic breaks, native-Windows blockers upstream reintroduced, the v3 artifact and a new chat template with its own quality screen, and a new checkpoint format.",
    "next": "Name every export-refusal gate on the shipped source with a diagnostic-only build, reproduce this window's shutdown refusal, then fix the gate so a graceful stop saves every live session.",
    "revisit_when": "An upstream change moves a lane gate when measured with scripts/engine_window_compare.py on the appliance, or the product needs a v3-only artifact or model. A trial merge is reproducible from the two recorded commits (fork d125ffffd87ef38d9a221f9830e19dfa274ddd34, upstream 594930e7b609efa4bcea3ae4f24cd9d66b5f224f)."
  },
